# Used only when the frontend is run in "worker" mode (see start-worker-app.bat at the
# repo root). This is what makes a copy of this frontend folder work correctly on a
# DIFFERENT physical laptop, away from the backend: instead of assuming the backend is on
# localhost (which only works when frontend + backend run on the SAME machine), it points
# at the public tunnel URL exposing your (Ritvik's) laptop's backend.
#
# One-time setup on Ritvik's laptop (see WORKER-LAPTOP-SETUP.md for full steps):
#   1. Sign up for a free ngrok account: https://dashboard.ngrok.com/signup
#   2. Install the ngrok agent and run: ngrok config add-authtoken <your-authtoken>
#   3. In the ngrok dashboard, go to Universal Gateway -> Domains and copy your free
#      permanent "dev domain" (looks like abc-123-xyz.ngrok-free.dev). Unlike the old
#      cloudflared quick tunnel this repo used before, this domain never changes.
#   4. Replace the placeholder below with that domain, then run start-worker-app.bat once
#      on THIS laptop to confirm it works, before copying the frontend folder over.
VITE_API_BASE=https://YOUR-NGROK-DOMAIN.ngrok-free.dev/api
